<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Kurwai State</h1><p class="st-meta">1713 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Kurwai</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Muslim-ruled state of central India, founded by an Afghan officer of the Mughals near Vidisha.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kurwai was founded in 1713 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-diler-khan">Muhammad Diler Khan</a>, an Afghan officer in Mughal service, who received the territory near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/betwa-river">Betwa</a> river. His descendants ruled as Nawabs.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Nawabs ruled a small territory of farming villages, much of it lost to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scindias">Sindhia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> in the 18th century. Under British paramountcy Kurwai was a minor state in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhopal-agency">Bhopal Agency</a>. Few further details are widely recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Kurwai joined <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/madhya-bharat">Madhya Bharat</a> in 1948 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a> in 1956. The town lies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidisha">Vidisha</a> district.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kurwai-state.jpg" alt="Kurwai State" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Germenfer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Kurwai_Princely_State.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1713 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kurwai</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Muhammad Diler Khan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam, Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hindi, Urdu</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kurwai</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1830&amp;focus=kurwai-state" aria-label="Kurwai State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6757 1289 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kurwai State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7077 1545L7364 1601M7077 1545L7364 1602M7077 1545L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7077 1545h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7077 1545h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1830&amp;focus=kurwai-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
